Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-23
Subject: Replace nobj's High(tequals) with the literal 1000
License: expat

`nobj.pas` allocates a workspace whose size is bounded by
`High(tequals)`. `tequals` is an enum that has been in flux across the
2.0.x series; pinning the bound to a literal `1000` keeps the
allocation independent of whatever `tequals`'s last member happens to
be in any given source tree.

--- a/compiler/nobj.pas
+++ b/compiler/nobj.pas
@@ -953,7 +953,7 @@
         cji: boolean;
       begin
         max:=_class.implementedinterfaces.count;
-        if max>High(tequals) then
+        if max>1000 then
           Internalerror(200006135);
         getmem(compats,sizeof(tcompintfentry)*max);
         getmem(equals,sizeof(longint)*max);
